# EMDR — mobile shell check

Any task that adds or changes a **page**, **layout**, **shell**, **nav/tabs**, or **page-level CSS** must be verified on a phone-width viewport before the turn ends.

## When this applies

- New or edited `page.tsx` / layout under `/app`, `/admin`, or the public site
- Shared chrome: sidebar, headers, tab bars, drawers, sticky bars, FABs
- CSS that affects page structure (`.settings-shell`, grids, flex shells, etc.)

Skip only for pure API/DB/logic with no UI surface.

## Required verification

1. Open the affected route on port **3471** (or tunnel).
2. Set viewport to **~390×844** (iPhone-class) — browser DevTools or CDP `Emulation.setDeviceMetricsOverride`.
3. Confirm with a **screenshot** and/or measured layout (`getBoundingClientRect` / computed styles), not desktop-only judgment.

## Pass criteria

- Content uses full width (no empty side column or squashed strip)
- Nav / tabs: readable; prefer horizontal scroll over chaotic wrap; active tab visible
- Sticky headers / back links do not overlap content
- Forms stack; no overflow-x on the page; primary actions reachable
- Safe-area + bottom padding so FABs (e.g. Help) do not cover controls
- No flex-wrap on a parent that mixes title, back link, and tab buttons

## Anti-patterns

```css
/* ❌ BAD — wraps Back + title + tabs together */
.settings-sidebar { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; }

/* ✅ GOOD — header block + separate scrollable nav */
.settings-sidebar-top { /* back + title */ }
.settings-nav { display: flex; flex-wrap: nowrap; overflow-x: auto; }
```

## Done bar

If you changed UI and did not run a mobile check, the task is **not done**. Say what viewport you used and what you saw.
